 formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(8)(4)-(-5)(3) \\\\  & =32+15 \\\\  & =47.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299592 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56075e41-2276-59fc-aa32-dc0aefbc46ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56075e41-2276-59fc-aa32-dc0aefbc46ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297914} :answer-field/id #uuid "9dd2ce63-3870-5dc7-88b5-af30fb44581f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299157}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51e6ce71-0f6b-5ca6-9047-0832d38b3af3" :question/math-academy-id "q-317336" :question/problem "Calculate $det(S)$ given that\n$S=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(S)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2)(3)-(4)(1) \\\\  & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6324678-0597-5421-a104-04c3342494f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6324678-0597-5421-a104-04c3342494f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298419} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfc4e21a-193b-52dd-8dc9-d21c2d8f7ddb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299337}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd3c7419-67b1-5120-a5e4-6bd19d8d0a71" :question/math-academy-id "q-317342" :question/problem "Calculate $det(S)$ given that\n$S=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(S)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(6)(7)-(-2)(5) \\\\  & =42+10 \\\\  & =52.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Integer Entries"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059749 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059558 :question/id #uuid "b066b73a-c777-550c-9c6e-af8093bf7fab" :question/math-academy-id "e-4435" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(A),$ if $[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}-(-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26e8a6ff-e5ed-59a7-b31d-1981495bf26a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050208 :topic/math-academy-id 362 :topic/title "The Power Rule for Exponents With Algebraic Expressions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051017 :topic/math-academy-id 353 :topic/title "Factoring Polynomials Using GCFs"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b466bee3-4694-50ff-b4ff-be40469939a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.typ